  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-forensic art direction, disciplined cyan/red palette, crisp card styling, and a compelling headline hierarchy across viewports. However, desktop and tablet composition leaves excessive dead space and weakens the narrative flow; tablet connectors feel detached, while mobile becomes a long stack with diminished visual drama. The desktop header’s oversized ghost lettering looks accidental, and the tiny, low-contrast navigation labels plus unresolved contrast evidence reduce polish.",
    "fix": "Tighten vertical rhythm, especially around the evidence diagram and footer; rebalance the tablet connectors and card positions; compress the mobile evidence sequence; remove or deliberately integrate the desktop header ghost lettering; and increase navigation label contrast and legibility.",
